  "source_description": "MIDCPNIFTY entry model, label=0.10% (5min horizon), trained 2026-09-12 as part of the multi-instrument feature-ceiling investigation: 47-feature OLD/ablation baseline -- old features beat new here (3rd different pattern across instruments), train 2026-02-02..2026-06-15, valid 2026-06-16..07-15, holdout 2026-07-16..08-06 (MIDCPNIFTY's own history is short, only ~7 months starting Feb 2026). Deployed at threshold 0.60 with EXIT_MAX_LOSS_PCT=0.01 (swept from default 0.10 -- MIDCPNIFTY wants a dramatically TIGHTER stop, the opposite direction from NIFTY and a much larger magnitude than BankNifty's own tightening, confirming this lever is genuinely instrument-specific in both direction and size). Real canonical backtest (2026-08-08..09-03, verified exact window): 13 live trades, 53.8% win, PF=4.84 after the stop sweep (3.26 at the old default) -- the strongest real result of the whole investigation by trade count and profit factor combined. NOT certified bug-free, and this candidate has NOT had the same direction-forensics review BankNifty/NIFTY got (deliberately deprioritized, not an oversight -- direction was already shown dead 3 independent ways on 2 other instruments). This is MIDCPNIFTY's FIRST EVER live deployment of any kind -- no prior trading history exists for this instrument. Deployed PAPER-ONLY: an operator_halt file was created proactively before first launch. IMPORTANT: the compose file's own '--rollout-stage paper' default does NOT actually gate real order execution for the deterministic engine (verified by reading strategy_app/main.py and risk/manager.py -- rollout_stage is only referenced by the retired ml_pure engine's runtime guard, not the deterministic engine every instrument actually runs) -- the operator_halt file is the real, code-enforced safety gate here, not the rollout-stage flag.",
